      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogy, didn't I? Sorry about that. Let's get back to the GDPR compliance advice.\n\nRegarding data security, you should implement technical and organizational measures to ensure the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of your customers' personal data. This includes:\n\n* Using secure protocols for data transmission (e.g., HTTPS)\n* Encrypting sensitive data (e.g., passwords, credit card numbers)\n* Implementing access controls and authentication mechanisms\n* Regularly updating and patching your systems to prevent vulnerabilities\n* Conducting regular security audits and risk assessments\n\nAs for data breaches, you should have a plan in place to respond quickly and effectively. This includes:\n\n* Notifying the affected individuals and the relevant authorities (e.g., CNIL) within 72 hours\n* Conducting an investigation to determine the cause of the breach\n* Implementing measures to prevent future breaches\n* Reviewing and updating your incident response plan\n\nIt's also essential to have a data protection officer (DPO) in place, especially if you're processing sensitive data. However, if you're a small online stationery shop, you might not need a DPO, but you should still have a clear understanding of your",
